{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729403Z","id":"7bec3684a53d4d228891f147137a443ef36e11d906cba05a2696681207c4cf0e","body":{"detail":"frameLoaded() closes the gate on a load with no hello, calls leaveDocument() (host.leave()), and asks the page to greet again with clax:greet. The page's hello reopens the gate, but the capability host starts over, so everything the page had set up through it ends and the page must set it up again. The spec states this as an open limitation (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-28-clax-design.md:1167-1171).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":624},"end":{"line":642},"content_hash":"72305be614779699d14d6ef0e341ca8695bf7df61efd86ed49f766a51dfdd6f9"},"suggested_fix":"When the hello that answers clax:greet comes from the same document (same artifact, version and file), keep or re-establish the host's room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors instead of starting over.","summary":"Back or Forward across a page's own fragments drops its room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/frame-host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730281Z","id":"4d1b4269e54dea08437973adcfaa170940e1002bace91f85d9601704550dd67a","body":{"detail":"With the viewer's activation, a subdomain-mode page can navigate the top window to another site or a fresh Clax load (docs/contract.md, Known limitations). Every load starts with the keyboard trail tainted, so what remains is C and ? live in the fresh load, and the navigation itself. Giving this frame sandbox='allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms allow-modals allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox allow-downloads' (no top navigation) would stop a navigation to another site; it needs every capability and page link checked first, and a popup the page opens keeps the shell's live keys either way. Decision needed: sandbox the subdomain frame or not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":61},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"431b45f7af17766e5236279b541ce64c1c05c8e23949fa4e3cd7257ec710cfa5"},"summary":"The subdomain-mode frame has no sandbox, so a page can navigate the whole window","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/trail.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730318Z","id":"2ae15dfc4b730f67ed2966a0113bcaa47b3ecf806ab2b2d73e3ad65874f37bea","body":{"detail":"No key clears the tainted trail, and every load starts tainted, so keyboard-only and screen-reader viewers need a pointer for Send, Resolve, Reply, the batch sends, a page-opened composer's Post, and the prompt's Allow. A path a page cannot coax (for example: the control held focus for ALLOW_DELAY_MS with no other key in between) would restore keyboard use. Decision needed: add such a path or not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":50},"content_hash":"6f6b435ae268b57cdf1b57ffc3db1fed62b7b5ee97e1f5ee6deedc2734083c92"},"summary":"No keyboard path for consequential actions once the trail is tainted","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","a11y","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/deltas.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731087Z","id":"3840a663992442d3b8d393dbb11a44ad1af9839c853aa64d6b44e0a1fa87264b","body":{"detail":"The artifact:<id> topic carries a thread's newest comment and its count; a view that missed a comment, or holds one deleted or edited before the newest, gets complete false and fetches that thread whole.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"dde23580758adb5c4ed4da369bdac4d1fbbfe066c2e5b056c20725d2c2610604"},"summary":"A thread delta whose comments do not add up fetches the thread whole","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731122Z","id":"93f0d25e0a13aee591cc4816b13d291787bc44c99eb625e669d011e2d9bbc274","body":{"detail":"A page's own publish (artifact.publish) moves every open unpinned view to the new version when the view hears its version event, which carries by_page (lines 115-128). A view whose stream goes live only after that publish learns of the version from this refetch on ready, which cannot tell who published, and offers Reload in the top bar. The browser tests wait for each view's stream before a vote (streamLive in web/e2e/fixtures.ts:203).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"a91a85289e6e1f0f950c25198984f37c048a7650c830e9460e903fe262484c32"},"summary":"A view that missed a page's publish offers Reload rather than following it","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731329Z","id":"76a00f1b49d5b22fa1e7deb61eece0b7ae52086b335bcdb05f2bc760a5b46906","body":{"detail":"After clax:degraded, the shell holds the part failed for that page: Comment stays off and says so, even once the bridge's own retry could load the part, and threads whose anchors went unanswered while it failed stay unplaced. This needs a protocol addition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1233},"end":{"line":1243},"content_hash":"d916958d7195a5a877a49f0b9d1b6e048afccef5dc947da03e0bf784247f5cbe"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a part that loads after failing; the shell then clears failedParts for it and its notice, and resolves the anchors again.","summary":"A lazy part that failed stays failed until the page's next hello, even once it loads","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/viewer-name-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183434Z","id":"96f44240940c1fa64105e9efc9072f147bf9e458a719255159c9bd5c73d8299f","body":{"detail":"save() runs for the Enter that saves the name and again for the Escape or blur that follows. Both pass the `next === this.saved` check before the first request answers (this.saved is set only in its .then), so the daemon receives the same rename twice and threads.ts announces the viewer twice. The stream hub ignores the repeated reconnect (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts, `reconnect` case), so the cost is one extra request and one extra announcement per rename.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"85e6dd8736724daec080d4f5e58dedddeb783098b0c4af3e77df622a1f99526f"},"suggested_fix":"Remember the name whose request is in flight and skip a save of the same name until it answers.","summary":"A rename can send two identical PUT /api/viewers/me requests","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:38:28.460502Z","id":"69abb375e48b9757b02124e6d05bf820e28c661a3a33cc98d15d34112f5cfbd5","body":{"detail":"A page's own publish (artifact.publish) moves every open unpinned view to the new version when the view hears its version event, which carries by_page (lines 115-128). A view whose stream goes live only after that publish learns of the version from this refetch on ready, which cannot tell who published, and offers Reload in the top bar. The browser tests wait for each view's stream before a vote (streamLive in web/e2e/fixtures.ts:203).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"a91a85289e6e1f0f950c25198984f37c048a7650c830e9460e903fe262484c32"},"summary":"A view that missed a page's publish offers Reload rather than following it","supersedes":"93f0d25e0a13aee591cc4816b13d291787bc44c99eb625e669d011e2d9bbc274","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
